     "type": "explanation",
     "name": "ROUGHNESS",
     "definition": "Roughness controls how the different 'octaves' of noise get scaled. Usually it is in the range [0,1] but it can be slightly higher or lower and still make sense (zero is actually a pretty decent value). The mathematical equation used is 2^(-k*(1-r)) where 'k' is the octave index starting at 0 and 'r' is the roughness value."
    },
    {
     "type": "struct",
     "name": "roughness",
     "definition": "scalar_function_struct_2"
    },
